# Line endings are a contract in this tree, not a preference.
#
# `ci/lint-line-endings.py` fails the gate on CRLF in any file a Linux shell,
# kernel or systemd will read (a shell script with CRLF fails at the shebang with
# an error that names the wrong file). The repository is edited on Windows, where
# the host's Git config had `core.autocrlf=true`: without this file, a checkout
# rewrites LF to CRLF and the defect appears without anyone editing the file.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the checkout to LF for every text file, on every host.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.fd binary
*.raw binary
*.qcow2 binary
*.iso binary
*.img binary
